1	//! How Qwen3 plugs into the engine contract — the whole adaptation, in one
2	//! file.
3	//!
4	//! [`Qwen3Scheduler`] implements [`pegainfer_frontend::engine::Scheduler`]:
5	//! the contract's driver polls `submit`/`step`/`metrics`; everything
6	//! south of here ([`crate::scheduler`], the executor) deals in the contract's
7	//! [`RequestId`] and pure effect data. This file owns the only two
8	//! contract-facing responsibilities:
9	//!
10	//! - the **ledger writes**: translating each step's effects into verdicts and
11	//!   tokens recorded on the [`RequestLedger`] by id;
12	//! - **engine assembly**: building the executor and returning the
13	//!   [`Engine`] bundle from `launch`.
14	//!
15	//! Cancellation is reactive: the frontend flips a request's abort flag and
16	//! this adapter retires it, at the top of the next step while it is queued or
17	//! waiting for its next prefill chunk, and on its next touch once it is
18	//! decoding or has a prefill in flight — the scheduler mechanics never see
19	//! aborts. Finishes ride the committed step unless the executor withholds
20	//! them ([`ModelExecutor::withholds_finishes`]): a P/D prefill executor takes
21	//! them as [`RequestLedger::defer_finish`] tokens and delivers each request's
22	//! final record once its KV saves are peer-visible.
